eyebrow: Guide · Sales
h1: Lead follow-up rules that stop solar leads leaking.
lead: Most lost leads were never rejected. They simply went quiet because nobody owned the next step. A few firm rules turn a pile of numbers into a pipeline.
answer: Give every lead one owner and one next date, check for duplicates on entry, log each call with its outcome, and review stale leads every week.
published: 2026-10-11
sections:
  - h: One owner per lead
    p:
      - A lead with two owners has none. Assign each enquiry to one person on the day it arrives. If someone else helps, add them as a collaborator, but keep one owner accountable.
  - h: Every lead has a next date
    p:
      - A lead without a next date is a lead you have forgotten. After each interaction, set the date of the next one, even if it is simply a call in a week.
  - h: Check for duplicates on entry
    p:
      - The same customer often arrives by call, walk-in and a dealer. Checking the phone number on entry avoids two people pitching the same house with different prices.
  - h: Log every call with an outcome
    p:
      - Use a short list of outcomes so the log is useful later.
    list:
      - Connected
      - Not answered
      - Busy
      - Wrong number
      - Call back later
    after: Record the next follow-up date in the same step, so the outcome and the next action are never separated.
  - h: Use a small number of statuses
    p:
      - A long status list is hard to maintain. Pick statuses that mark real changes, such as new, contacted, survey scheduled, quoted, negotiating, won and lost, and give each a clear meaning.
  - h: Record why you lost
    p:
      - A lost lead with a reason teaches something. After a month you will see whether you lose on price, timing or service area.
  - h: Review stale leads weekly
    p:
      - Every week, list the leads with no activity for seven days or whose next date has passed. Assign each one a decision, which is to call, reassign or close.
takeaways:
  - One owner and one next date for every lead.
  - Duplicate check on entry, outcome on every call.
  - Weekly sweep of stale leads.
